1
00:00:22,001 --> 00:00:24,371
A TRUE WARRIOR

2
00:00:43,391 --> 00:00:45,601
Don't get cocky.

3
00:01:03,041 --> 00:01:04,581
Who is he?

4
00:01:18,971 --> 00:01:19,801
He's coming.

5
00:01:20,851 --> 00:01:22,261
What are we going to do, Bjorn?

6
00:01:53,801 --> 00:01:57,261
This is bad. Bjorn's gone mad.

7
00:02:01,801 --> 00:02:03,931
Stop him. He'll destroy the ship.

8
00:02:04,011 --> 00:02:06,311
You're crazy.

9
00:02:06,391 --> 00:02:08,941
How are we supposed to stop a monster like that?

10
00:02:09,021 --> 00:02:11,811
Run. No one can stop him now.

11
00:02:18,361 --> 00:02:20,991
He's eaten a berserker mushroom.

12
00:02:53,811 --> 00:02:55,571
All with his bare hands...

13
00:02:55,861 --> 00:02:58,281
He's stronger than a monster.

14
00:02:59,031 --> 00:03:01,991
The Troll of Jom.

15
00:03:04,781 --> 00:03:07,371
All right. One more ship.

16
00:03:18,591 --> 00:03:20,341
They're here.

17
00:03:20,421 --> 00:03:22,641
-What are we going to do?
-Surrender?

18
00:03:25,721 --> 00:03:28,311
Damn it. Come on.

19
00:03:28,391 --> 00:03:30,641
I'd rather die fighting than be a slave.

20
00:03:30,731 --> 00:03:33,901
Listen. Capture the kids alive.

21
00:03:33,981 --> 00:03:37,651
If they get hurt, they won't sell for a high price.
Be careful.

22
00:03:47,281 --> 00:03:49,541
We're going to have some fun with you.

23
00:03:57,841 --> 00:03:59,051
Bjorn?

24
00:04:07,391 --> 00:04:08,311
Thors.

25
00:04:17,861 --> 00:04:21,991
Listen. You've already lost half of your forces.

26
00:04:22,651 --> 00:04:25,661
Leave now, and I won't take your life.

27
00:06:04,841 --> 00:06:06,761
Be gone, pirates.

28
00:06:06,841 --> 00:06:08,841
You cannot defeat me.

29
00:06:10,471 --> 00:06:12,471
-That bastard.
-Stop.

30
00:06:12,851 --> 00:06:15,721
Don't shoot until Askeladd gives the signal.

31
00:06:16,021 --> 00:06:17,771
What are they doing?

32
00:06:17,851 --> 00:06:19,691
We've got the high ground.

33
00:06:19,771 --> 00:06:21,611
What are they stalling for?

34
00:06:23,401 --> 00:06:25,611
What a crazy man.

35
00:06:26,111 --> 00:06:29,611
He's not afraid to take on two whole warships alone.

36
00:06:30,071 --> 00:06:31,701
Let's fight too.

37
00:06:31,781 --> 00:06:34,581
Fool. You amateurs will make things worse.

38
00:06:35,331 --> 00:06:37,911
Their archers are waiting up on the cliff.

39
00:06:38,581 --> 00:06:41,581
He's the one who knows how to handle this.

40
00:06:41,671 --> 00:06:43,591
But...

41
00:06:43,841 --> 00:06:45,211
Don't you understand?

42
00:06:45,301 --> 00:06:46,841
Except for Thors,

43
00:06:46,921 --> 00:06:49,301
we're just a bunch of kids and amateurs.

44
00:06:49,971 --> 00:06:52,181
All we can do is let him handle this.

45
00:06:57,271 --> 00:07:01,561
It looks like they're not
the type of men to leave when I say so.

46
00:07:02,101 --> 00:07:05,071
The archers up on the cliff aren't firing yet.

47
00:07:05,731 --> 00:07:07,781
There's 30 men to the front.

48
00:07:07,861 --> 00:07:10,321
I know I could kill that many myself.

49
00:07:11,281 --> 00:07:13,321
But our ships are close.

50
00:07:13,571 --> 00:07:17,201
If they all jumped over to our ship,
it'd be a free-for-all.

51
00:07:18,661 --> 00:07:20,661
I'd be fine if I was alone, but...

52
00:07:32,261 --> 00:07:33,641
Are you the leader?

53
00:07:34,681 --> 00:07:37,011
In the name of Odin, the Almighty,

54
00:07:37,101 --> 00:07:39,101
I challenge you to a duel.

55
00:07:42,771 --> 00:07:45,191
If you win, you can do whatever you want.

56
00:07:45,271 --> 00:07:48,231
If I win, you must withdraw at once.

57
00:07:48,321 --> 00:07:49,901
If you refuse,

58
00:07:49,991 --> 00:07:52,991
then you're going to lose three times as many men

59
00:07:53,071 --> 00:07:55,701
to capture a mere 12 slaves.

60
00:08:00,541 --> 00:08:02,331
Can I ask you something?

61
00:08:03,541 --> 00:08:05,541
Why do you think I'm their leader?

62
00:08:10,671 --> 00:08:11,631
I can smell it.

63
00:08:14,181 --> 00:08:15,801
Impressive.

64
00:08:16,391 --> 00:08:18,971
All right. I accept the duel.

65
00:08:19,431 --> 00:08:23,311
I, Askeladd, son of Olaf, swear in the name of Odin.

66
00:08:23,981 --> 00:08:26,061
Stay back near the ship's bow.

67
00:08:26,151 --> 00:08:27,561
Okay.

68
00:08:45,751 --> 00:08:46,881
I too

69
00:08:47,921 --> 00:08:50,751
can smell something about you.

70
00:08:51,341 --> 00:08:53,131
You have the same smell as me,

71
00:08:53,761 --> 00:08:55,681
Troll of Jom.

72
00:08:57,051 --> 00:08:58,301
He knows who I am?

73
00:09:00,681 --> 00:09:01,891
Did Floki do this?

74
00:09:03,181 --> 00:09:06,771
You're quick. I like smart men.

75
00:09:07,151 --> 00:09:10,441
My father isn't a bad man like you.

76
00:09:10,521 --> 00:09:11,861
Hey. Stay back.

77
00:09:11,941 --> 00:09:14,951
My father is strong. Die, you pirate.

78
00:09:15,031 --> 00:09:17,111
You idiot. You idiot. Your armor looks weird.

79
00:09:18,571 --> 00:09:21,161
What an energetic boy. Is that your son?

80
00:09:22,541 --> 00:09:24,451
Stop. You fool.

81
00:09:24,541 --> 00:09:27,421
Askeladd. Do you have a wife and children?

82
00:09:29,081 --> 00:09:29,961
No.

83
00:09:31,711 --> 00:09:32,711
I see.

84
00:09:34,421 --> 00:09:35,421
Let's begin.

85
00:09:46,061 --> 00:09:48,981
He's closing up the distance carelessly.

86
00:10:18,181 --> 00:10:19,011
Too shallow.

87
00:10:29,351 --> 00:10:30,851
You're amazing.

88
00:10:30,941 --> 00:10:33,481
No one can beat Askeladd.

89
00:10:34,071 --> 00:10:35,691
Father.

90
00:10:39,111 --> 00:10:42,241
He dodged it. My moment of opportunity...

91
00:10:42,871 --> 00:10:45,331
A surprise attack won't work on him anymore.

92
00:10:45,871 --> 00:10:50,001
Coming all this way was worth it.

93
00:10:50,461 --> 00:10:53,211
He's an incredible man.

94
00:10:53,881 --> 00:10:55,211
Thors...

95
00:10:56,671 --> 00:10:57,881
You're strong.

96
00:11:02,971 --> 00:11:04,641
Forgive me, Askeladd.

97
00:11:05,311 --> 00:11:06,891
I can't go easy on you.

98
00:11:08,311 --> 00:11:10,891
I'm happy to hear that, Thors.

99
00:11:24,201 --> 00:11:25,241
What?

100
00:11:25,331 --> 00:11:26,411
Hey, hey.

101
00:11:42,261 --> 00:11:44,341
Amazing. It's a one-sided fight.

102
00:11:46,761 --> 00:11:49,021
Askeladd is in trouble.

103
00:11:49,101 --> 00:11:52,481
But he's able to block all his attacks.

104
00:11:52,851 --> 00:11:55,981
Father. Kill him.

105
00:12:01,281 --> 00:12:02,281
Oh, no.

106
00:12:02,951 --> 00:12:06,161
He's going after my sword. It won't hold up for long.

107
00:12:07,911 --> 00:12:09,161
That must mean...

108
00:12:09,241 --> 00:12:10,621
His sword is also...

109
00:12:12,961 --> 00:12:14,001
This is it.

110
00:12:19,591 --> 00:12:21,761
Since I know his target,

111
00:12:21,841 --> 00:12:24,471
I can predict the arc of his sword.

112
00:12:24,551 --> 00:12:26,471
This is it. A wide swing.

113
00:12:33,811 --> 00:12:35,441
I fell for his trap.

114
00:12:35,521 --> 00:12:38,401
He was waiting for me to get careless,
and swing wide.

115
00:12:38,691 --> 00:12:41,321
He was planning to have me snap his sword,
all along.

116
00:12:41,401 --> 00:12:43,651
Everything went according to his plan.

117
00:12:44,031 --> 00:12:45,531
Unbelievable.

118
00:12:45,611 --> 00:12:48,451
I can't believe I fell for it.

119
00:12:49,121 --> 00:12:50,541
You did it.

120
00:12:50,621 --> 00:12:54,161
-Thors. You did it.
-That was amazing, Father.

121
00:12:54,251 --> 00:12:55,541
You won.

122
00:13:00,211 --> 00:13:02,421
What's wrong? Kill me.

123
00:13:03,471 --> 00:13:05,381
I don't need to.

124
00:13:05,471 --> 00:13:07,551
Say you surrender. That's enough for me.

125
00:13:09,681 --> 00:13:11,561
I'm their leader.

126
00:13:12,181 --> 00:13:14,561
I can't say that in front of my men.

127
00:13:22,821 --> 00:13:24,821
What's wrong? Kill me.

128
00:13:24,901 --> 00:13:26,661
If you don't kill me,

129
00:13:26,741 --> 00:13:28,871
this duel will never end.

130
00:13:39,041 --> 00:13:42,001
Ouch, my head hurts.

131
00:13:45,801 --> 00:13:48,971
What? What's going on?

132
00:13:54,391 --> 00:13:55,521
Askeladd...

133
00:13:56,561 --> 00:13:57,601
Defeat?

134
00:13:58,311 --> 00:13:59,901
He lost?

135
00:14:00,561 --> 00:14:03,861
Admit it. I won this duel.

136
00:14:03,941 --> 00:14:05,531
Withdraw your troops at once.

137
00:14:07,651 --> 00:14:09,781
You really are strong, Thors.

138
00:14:10,241 --> 00:14:12,911
You could lead a whole army.

139
00:14:15,251 --> 00:14:17,041
But why?

140
00:14:17,121 --> 00:14:21,171
Why did you stay in Iceland for 15 years,
even though you're such a strong warrior?

141
00:14:21,841 --> 00:14:23,801
Don't you think you're wasting your skills?

142
00:14:24,131 --> 00:14:25,301
No.

143
00:14:28,801 --> 00:14:31,261
I must rely on a sword like this,

144
00:14:32,351 --> 00:14:34,311
because I am not yet a master.

145
00:14:35,971 --> 00:14:37,771
A true warrior

146
00:14:38,231 --> 00:14:39,481
doesn't need a sword.

147
00:14:51,741 --> 00:14:53,201
Thors, you...

148
00:14:54,701 --> 00:14:56,701
Why don't you become our leader?

149
00:15:16,561 --> 00:15:19,231
Just kidding. Hey, hey.

150
00:15:19,311 --> 00:15:21,731
Why isn't anyone laughing? I was just joking.

151
00:15:24,311 --> 00:15:26,361
What? He was joking?

152
00:15:28,191 --> 00:15:30,991
This is no time for...

153
00:15:31,071 --> 00:15:33,991
joking around with a straight face.

154
00:15:38,581 --> 00:15:40,371
Don't move.

155
00:15:40,461 --> 00:15:42,791
I'll cut the kid's head off.

156
00:15:42,871 --> 00:15:44,131
Let go of your sword.

157
00:15:44,211 --> 00:15:45,921
Hurry up.

158
00:15:47,421 --> 00:15:49,261
Askeladd. You bastard.

159
00:15:50,471 --> 00:15:52,511
Father.

160
00:15:58,601 --> 00:16:00,891
Come on. You're such a good man.

161
00:16:01,561 --> 00:16:04,401
Did you think we were going
to follow the rules of the duel?

162
00:16:07,651 --> 00:16:10,321
I was just playing around with you.

163
00:16:10,401 --> 00:16:13,951
I wanted to find out
how good the famous Troll of Jom really was.

164
00:16:14,031 --> 00:16:15,701
I had a good time.

165
00:16:39,261 --> 00:16:40,221
Askeladd.

166
00:16:41,221 --> 00:16:43,851
You broke the rules of the duel.

167
00:16:44,561 --> 00:16:46,731
I won this match.

168
00:16:48,521 --> 00:16:50,071
Who cares?

169
00:16:50,151 --> 00:16:52,571
I'm after your head.

170
00:16:53,701 --> 00:16:54,701
I know.

171
00:17:14,971 --> 00:17:16,221
I accept.

172
00:17:18,851 --> 00:17:20,391
The winner of this duel...

173
00:17:22,271 --> 00:17:23,891
is you.

174
00:17:35,281 --> 00:17:39,571
Father!

175
00:17:53,211 --> 00:17:54,421
Father...

176
00:17:56,931 --> 00:17:58,591
Askeladd.

177
00:17:58,681 --> 00:18:00,971
I won this duel.

178
00:18:02,181 --> 00:18:04,601
Keep the promise you made as a warrior.

179
00:18:06,681 --> 00:18:07,941
I know.

180
00:18:08,021 --> 00:18:10,811
In the name of my ancestor Artorius,

181
00:18:10,901 --> 00:18:12,691
I shall withdraw my troops at once.

182
00:18:17,611 --> 00:18:20,951
Leif. I have a favor to ask you.

183
00:18:23,581 --> 00:18:26,661
Bring my head to Sigvaldi,

184
00:18:26,751 --> 00:18:28,961
the leader of the Jomsvikings.

185
00:18:29,501 --> 00:18:33,461
If he suspects that I disappeared
to avoid his summons,

186
00:18:33,801 --> 00:18:35,841
he'll take his revenge by punishing the village.

187
00:18:36,801 --> 00:18:38,721
You're a crazy man.

188
00:18:44,811 --> 00:18:46,391
You bastard.

189
00:18:46,931 --> 00:18:49,851
I'll give you my life. Just like you wanted.

190
00:18:50,901 --> 00:18:52,861
Let that child go right now.

191
00:18:56,691 --> 00:18:59,281
Father. Father.

192
00:19:18,631 --> 00:19:19,671
I'm glad.

193
00:19:21,091 --> 00:19:22,341
For now...

194
00:19:39,821 --> 00:19:41,491
Damn kid.

195
00:19:42,241 --> 00:19:44,621
You should start valuing your life.

196
00:19:45,491 --> 00:19:47,871
You should be grateful to Thors.

197
00:19:47,951 --> 00:19:51,921
He was a man who was worth more
than a hundred bratty kids like you.

198
00:20:06,261 --> 00:20:08,471
Father died.

199
00:20:10,521 --> 00:20:12,941
Father was so strong.

200
00:20:14,851 --> 00:20:16,691
Why did he let go of his sword?

201
00:20:17,731 --> 00:20:20,571
How could he say a warrior doesn't need a sword?

202
00:20:21,611 --> 00:20:23,571
That can't be true.

203
00:20:25,911 --> 00:20:27,741
Why...?

204
00:20:27,831 --> 00:20:29,541
Why did Father...?

205
00:20:30,831 --> 00:20:32,621
Damn.

206
00:20:32,711 --> 00:20:34,461
He...

207
00:20:34,541 --> 00:20:36,831
He lost to Father.

208
00:20:36,921 --> 00:20:38,801
Damn it.

209
00:20:38,881 --> 00:20:40,961
Why was my father the one who died?

210
00:20:41,051 --> 00:20:43,341
Why is he the one who's still alive?

211
00:20:44,181 --> 00:20:45,341
Damn it.

212
00:20:46,391 --> 00:20:48,181
Damn it all.

213
00:20:56,441 --> 00:20:58,821
I'm surprised they abandoned these nice ships.

214
00:20:58,901 --> 00:21:00,981
It must have been a big decision.

215
00:21:01,071 --> 00:21:04,361
They can't move the ship without Thors.

216
00:21:04,451 --> 00:21:07,161
Thors could row as hard as five men.

217
00:21:07,241 --> 00:21:08,571
Really?

218
00:21:11,741 --> 00:21:13,711
Things worked out well.

219
00:21:13,791 --> 00:21:15,541
I was wanting to get a third ship.

220
00:21:22,461 --> 00:21:24,631
Twenty-eight men injured.

221
00:21:24,721 --> 00:21:25,551
How many died?

222
00:21:26,631 --> 00:21:29,891
None? Not even one? Impossible.

223
00:21:32,521 --> 00:21:33,851
Askeladd.

224
00:21:34,481 --> 00:21:35,441
Hey.

225
00:21:35,941 --> 00:21:39,151
Come to the stern. Askeladd.

226
00:21:39,611 --> 00:21:42,731
What do you want? Shut up already.

227
00:21:51,911 --> 00:21:53,411
It's Thors' kid.

228
00:21:53,791 --> 00:21:55,791
He was hiding inside the ship.

229
00:21:55,871 --> 00:22:00,081
Look at him. The kid's got a dagger.

230
00:22:00,171 --> 00:22:04,711
He's going to kill us.

231
00:22:07,631 --> 00:22:10,551
Oh, no. I'm so scared.

232
00:22:11,971 --> 00:22:13,311
How dare you...?

233
00:22:14,721 --> 00:22:15,851
How dare you...?

234
00:22:15,931 --> 00:22:19,311
How dare you kill Father?

235
00:22:20,191 --> 00:22:22,151
I'm going to kill you.

236
00:22:22,231 --> 00:22:24,481
I'm going to kill you, no matter what.

237
00:22:24,571 --> 00:22:27,201
I'm going to kill you!

238
00:22:29,161 --> 00:22:32,831
I'm going to kill you!

239
00:22:35,831 --> 00:22:36,951
He's just a kid.

240
00:22:37,041 --> 00:22:39,581
But that look in his eyes...

241
00:22:42,541 --> 00:22:44,801
What do you want to do, Askeladd?

242
00:22:44,881 --> 00:22:46,591
Shall we throw him overboard?

243
00:22:48,591 --> 00:22:49,971
Leave him.

244
00:22:51,391 --> 00:22:53,011
He will die soon anyway.

245
00:23:00,811 --> 00:23:02,111
Father...
